the World of Tanks development team  continued improving our project  throughout 2013 these improvements  touched on many different aspects of the  game now it's time to shed some light on  the details of the progress we're making  in this video we will tell you about how  the game physics is about to change  Sigmund Freud the founding father of  psychoanalysis considered the passion  for Destruction  a normal feature of the human psyche we  also understand this passion that's why  we've decided to bring the in-game  destruction system to a new level we've  been experimenting with this system for  more than a year all destructible  buildings have been remade now buildings  don't simply change from one condition  to another they do it in a beautiful way  wooden houses break into logs frail  Hut's fall into pieces brick walls crack  along the brickwork joints when a  building is destroyed you may see an  entire wall topple at the ground and  smash itself into smaller fragments  these fragments can also interact with  vehicles and be destroyed as well we try  different detail levels of destruction  of brick buildings big fragments small  fragments a combination of big and small  fragments we even created a model of a  building that literally breaks apart  into single bricks the way a building  can be destroyed depends not only on the  type of material it is built up but also  on the type of shell that hits it an  armor-piercing shell will just pierce a  hole in the wall while the blast of a  high-explosive shell will scatter pieces  in all directions  buildings can be complex  for example two-story you can fire at  the first storey and it will be  destroyed then the second storey will  also collapse some in-game objects  cannot be destroyed due to gameplay  requirements it must exist however they  also have some elements that can be  disrupted you can shoot off a balcony or  break glass all this became possible due  to the introduction of the havok  physic's engine this software is used in  the gaming and film industries to create  special effects of course havoc will not  only be used for the building  destruction system we decided to go  further and provide vehicles with  physically correct behavior now all  elements of Tanks including side panels  from tennis and chains naturally rock  and dangle when vehicles are moving they  can be lost during combat action for  example when tanks collide they can also  be shot off by enemies the most  significant changes will be to vehicle  suspensions now wheels will roll over  uneven terrain in a natural way the t26  was probably the most difficult tank to  remake it has a double suspension that  consists of several suspension arms so  its behavior is quite complex  however we were successful but despite  the move ability and accuracy of the new  suspension something in its behavior  seemed to still be wrong the problem was  the tracks we built a new model to  simulate tracks without using any third  party instruments every single track  element is now calculated and animated  separately work on tracks continues the  next step is to make their behavior  realistic not only in motion but also  when they are knocked off droop off the  wheel unreal and so on with the  introduction of client physics what  players have long wanted will finally  come true World of Tanks will utilize  multiple processor cores havoc will take  full advantage of the computing power of  multi-core processors however players  will be able to turn this feature off on  computers with low performance  characteristics but the game will remain  the same for them because server-side  physics will change as well our work  making vehicles behave more  realistically led to the development of  a new model of Tanks powertrain this  model simulates the work of the whole  mechanism from clutch to wheels even  mechanical losses are taken into account  transmission gears change when a vehicle  is on the move now tanks behave like  real combat vehicles to the last detail  of course players will need some time to  get used to the new behavior of the  vehicles players won't experience any  technical difficulties though such  action is as gear change or smooth  depression of the clutch pedal will be  controlled automatically by your in-game  driver improvement of the physical model  of the powertrain yielded interesting  results now interaction between vehicles  and terrain can be simulated more  accurately the current physics model  provides only one settable parameter  rolling resistance it influences how  fast a vehicle gathers speed and what  it's top speed is accurate simulation of  the powertrain and the new physics  system allows us to consider many more  parameters of terrain besides the  already existing rolling resistance  traction and terrain deformation  parameters will also be considered this  means that vehicles will behave  differently depending on the type of  terrain this difference will show an  acceleration time slipping and side-wise  skidding changes in the way suspension  Springs work will also be included in  the more realistic physics engine in the  new model the stiffness of the springs  depends on degree of compression  this means that Springs are quite smooth  when there's little compression and this  allows driving over small bumps without  rocking but when bouncing over larger  bumps Springs will behave as stiff  suspension Beauty changes in server-side  physics tank turrets can now be blown  off the first challenge was that there  was no separate turret in the  homogeneous collision models of Tanks  then as the turret became a separate  model we experimented with tearing it  away just by applying some momentum it  could fly away by dozens of meters it  looked funny but completely unnatural  so work continued there are many things  to be considered for the turret to  behave realistically when applying  initial impulse in the end we ended up  taking into account the internal volume  of the tank we also consider the volume  of remaining ammunition and even the  type of ammunition when the turret comes  off destruction of its base is uneven  and circumferential it's damaged heavier  at some points and less at others  initial angular velocity or in other  words how the turret will spin in the  air is determined by where the turret  attachment is weaker after the turret  comes off it exists as a material body  with its own mass it can serve as cover  it can fall down and cause damage or  destroy a building or damage a vehicle  it can even destroy a vehicle so beware  of flying turrets the changes we made in  order to implement the tangible turrets  led to changes and another aspect of the  game players will now be able to move  various objects these can include trucks  trolley cars wagons or even an entire  train some cars can be moved as well if  they're big enough the behavior of  trucks is worth mentioning we're rather  proud of this feature trucks in the game  have soft suspensions wheels are  spring-loaded the front axle can turn  so if you somehow move a truck and its  front axle turns and then you push it  from behind the truck will roll in a  curve only if its front axle straightens  out will it move straight some buildings  are still indestructible but this may  change one day we're also experimenting  with server-side realistic destruction  of large objects we already have a  technology that allows buildings to  break into fragments and finally there  is another feature that will affect the  behavior of tanks now they can flip over  we could have implemented this feature  long ago together with falling off the  hills unfortunately the game wasn't  ready for this then for such an advanced  technology so I had to impose a maximum  rotation of 60 degrees so the tanks  couldn't turn over now we're completely  ready for turnovers so all I have to do  is remove this restriction this is all  for now we have told you about the most  important upcoming changes to world of  tanks physics follow the news we got  more surprises for you good luck on the  battlefield
 

